RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
June 25, 2012
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date beginning
at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL
MEMBERS - Mr. Allen, Ms. Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Collins, Mr. Pierson,  Dr. Rinne,
Mr. Spiker and Mr. Valdez.  Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Lois Huff, City Treasurer,
and Dan White, City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and support by two
other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its
normal sequence on the agenda.)  Upon request by Mr. Brown, and pursuant to support received by
Mr. Collins and Ms. Ash,  agenda item #18 was removed from the Consent Agenda.  Mr. Collins
moved to approve remaining Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on June 11, 2012.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
Minutes from Special Session of the Governing Body on June 19, 2012.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Brown and Mr. Collins  each  declared a conflict of interest (business interest in
vouchers payable to Ameri-Tech HVAC Services and the Bicycle Station, Inc. respectively) and
vacated Council Chambers.  Mr. Valdez moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented,
seconded by Mr. Allen.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present
in Council Chambers.  Following announcement of the vote, Mr. Brown and Mr. Collins returned
to Council Chambers.
Mayor Kaysen opened a public hearing to receive comments and input for a transfer of
ownership and transfer of location for a retail liquor license filed with the City Clerk’s Office by
Steamboat’s LLC d/b/a Steamboat’s Wyoming Steak and Smoke House, 1947 Dell Range
Boulevard, Cheyenne, Wyoming (License currently held by Let ’er Buck Investment Group LLC
d/b/a Steamboat’s, (address not yet issued) to be located off Gardenia Drive between Yellowstone
Road and El Camino Real in Cathedral Commons).  Upon inquiry,  James Yates, applicant member,
confirmed the proposed new business location is the former Shari’s restaurant building on Dell
Range and provided information on the transfer of ownership, explaining that some of the partners
in Steamboat’s LLC are the same as those with Let ’er Buck Investment Group LLC.  There being
no further comments and purpose of the hearing having been met, Mayor Kaysen closed the hearing
and referred the application to Finance Committee.
Ordinance amending Ordinance No. 3925 defining the terms and conditions of employment
for non-uniformed employees of the City of Cheyenne.  Reporting for Finance Committee, Mr.
```

