Brown moved to approve on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Pierson.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body. (#3951)
Ordinance amending Ordinance No. 3926 defining the terms and conditions of employment
for sworn officers of the City of Cheyenne Police Department.  Mr. Brown moved to approve on
third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Valdez.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of
the governing body. (#3952)
Ordinance pursuant to Section 2.2.1 Zoning Map Amendments, Section 5.1.2 Zoning
Districts Established and Section 5.1.3 Official Zoning Map (Cheyenne City Map), of the Unified
Development Code, changing the zoning classification from HR-2 High Density Residential-
Developing District to MR-2 Medium-Density Residential-Developing District for Lot 21, Block
14, Saddle Ridge, Cheyenne, Wyoming, to be known as a portion of Saddle Ridge, Fourth Filing
(located at the southeast corner of the intersection of Whitney Road and Countryside Avenue).
Reporting for Public Services Committee, Ms. Ash moved to approve on second reading, seconded
by Ms. Broyles.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.
Ordinance pursuant to Section 2.2.1 Zoning Map Amendments, Section 5.1.2 Zoning
Districts Established and Section 5.1.3 Official Zoning Map (Cheyenne City Map), of the Unified
Development Code, changing the zoning classification from CB Community Business District to
LI Light Industrial District for Lots 2, 3, and 4, Block 397, Original City, Cheyenne, Wyoming
(located at the southeast corner of the intersection of Dillon Avenue and W. 17 Street).  Ms. Ash
th
moved to approve on second reading, seconded by Ms. Broyles.  Comments followed regarding
discussion held at the Public Services Committee meeting concerning whether a zoning condition
should be considered with regard to outside storage.  Discussion included the following topics:
Expressions that a zoning condition would not be necessary; flexibility involving uses within the
proposed LI zoned classification for the area; limited outside storage space impact to the
neighborhood due to the building located on the site; PlanCheyenne and the downtown area;
reconsidering the Unified Development Code as written; other LI zoned area(s) in the vicinity, and
consistency with uses for businesses in the area.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of
the governing body.
Ordinance annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a parcel of land being situated in
a portion of the North Half of the North Half of the Northeast Quarter of the Northeast Quarter of
Section 11, Township 13 North, Range 67 West of the 6th P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming
(generally located at the I-25/I-80 Interchange, a.k.a. 4121 W. 5th Street).  Ms. Ash moved to
approve on second reading, seconded by Ms. Broyles.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” --  all members
of the governing body.
Ordinance granting a Franchise by the City of Cheyenne to High West Energy, Inc., its
successors and assigns, the right to furnish, sell and distribute electricity to the City and all persons,
businesses, and industry within a portion of the City High West’s certificated territory and the right
to acquire, construct, install, locate, maintain, operate and extend into, within and through said City
all facilities reasonably necessary to furnish, sell and distribute electricity within the City and the
right to make reasonable use of all streets and other public places and public easements as herein
defined as may be necessary; and fixing the terms and conditions thereof -- referred to Finance
Committee (sponsors -- Ms. Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Pierson).
