Announcement was made of a Public Hearing to be held July 9, 2012 at 6:00 p.m. in City
Council Chambers, 2101 O'Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming, for a restaurant liquor license
application filed with the City Clerk's Office for 2 Doors Down 2, Inc. d/b/a 2 Doors Down 2, 1802
Dell Range Boulevard, Suite 2, Cheyenne, Wyoming.
Announcement was made of the Appointment of Brandon Kramer to the the Downtown
Development Authority Board to be confirmed July 9, 2012.
Announcement was made that two Calcuttas, benefitting the Cheyenne Frontier Days
Scholarship Program, will be held as follows: Thursday, July 19, 2012 beginning at 7:00 p.m. at The
Redwood Lounge, 2105 East Lincolnway, in conjunction with the Cheyenne Frontier Days Wild
Horse Races to be held July 21-29, 2012 at Frontier Park, and Saturday, July 28, 2012 beginning at
8:00 p.m. at the Redwood Lounge, 2105 East Lincolnway, in conjunction with the Cheyenne
Frontier Days Wild Horse Race to be held July 29, 2012 at Frontier Park, Cheyenne, Wyoming, in
conjunction with the 2012 Cheyenne Frontier Days celebration (15% of proceeds to CFD
Scholarship Program).

Announcement was made that the local Wyoming Chapter for Multiple Sclerosis (MS) will
be sponsoring a Calcutta to be held Thursday, August 16, 2012 beginning at 6:00 p.m. at Alf’s Pub
and Package Liquor, 1622 East 19th Street, Cheyenne, Wyoming, in conjunction with the MS
Society/Alf’s Pub Golf Tournament (15% of proceeds to benefit the local MS Society).
Under other business, Larry Proietti expressed concerns regarding a political candidate
signboard displayed in Lions Park during the Superday event on June 23rd).  Upon request, Rick
Parish, Parks and Recreation Director, advised the vehicle that had the signboard displayed was a
